bcachefs 1.36.1 (DKMS): the inode state helpers are in Linux 6.18.64

bcachefs defines inode_state_read, inode_state_read_once and inode_state_set_raw itself on kernels older than 6.19,
which introduced them. Linux 6.18.64 (stable) brought them back to 6.18, so on 6.18.64 they are defined twice and the
module does not build (with Void's 6.18.64 kernel as with Ribbon's). bcachefs-tools 1.39.7 has the same guard. With
this, bcachefs's own definitions are for kernels older than 6.18.64. build/ci/kernel.sh applies it before DKMS builds
the module, and stops when it does not apply.

--- a/src/fs/bcachefs/vfs/fs.c
+++ b/src/fs/bcachefs/vfs/fs.c
@@ -48,7 +48,7 @@
 #include <linux/version.h>
 #include <linux/xattr.h>
 
-#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(6,19,0)
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(6,18,64)
 static inline unsigned inode_state_read(struct inode *inode)
 {
 	return inode->i_state;
